# Air-gapped pip/uv mirror seam for the k3s profile (and any shell that runs
# `pip install` / `uv pip install` by hand). Export these in that shell; fill
# in the real mirror URLs there.
#
# The single-node profile does NOT use this file: it has ONE seam,
# CC_PYPI_INDEX_URL in deploy/single/.env, which setup.sh fans out to every
# name below — because the two tools do not share configuration. uv reads
# no PIP_* variable and no pip.conf (its config pages mention neither), and
# UV_INDEX_URL is DEPRECATED in favour of UV_DEFAULT_INDEX (since uv 0.4.23;
# the old name still works with a warning). Setting only the pip name leaves
# uv on the public index, silently, until it times out.

# PIP_INDEX_URL=https://MIRROR_HOST/pypi/simple
# UV_DEFAULT_INDEX=https://MIRROR_HOST/pypi/simple
# UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_MIRROR=https://MIRROR_HOST/python-build-standalone
